  "title": "Transitive consciousness and consciousness in general",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "6d62635a-3931-40e4-a983-6e2ff5b11e43",
      "text": "Transitive visual consciousness is being visually aware of a feature of a scene. Visual consciousness in general is the higher-order capacity to become aware of present features, which contrasts with being asleep or blind.",
